I will always save a place in my heart for LISA, one of my personal game of all time. I absolutely love original games, and this title plays beautifully with that notion. In a world where women are inexistent, men are completely mad and so is the gory planet where they live.
Featuring the journey of a broken and addicted man to find Buddy, his "daughter", and save her from the ♥♥♥♥ed up world that surrounds them.
- Pros:
+ Different concept of a post apocalyptic world, where only men prevailed, and are threatened to be extinct to due lack of procreation;
+ Interesting set of characters;
+ Huge variety of events, some hidden;
+ 3 endings: Joyful, Joyless, and Pain mode;
+ Pleasant variety of companions;
+ 58 achievements to complete;
+ Existence of a drug codenamed Joy, and compelling mutants that result from it's abuse;
+ Original status ailments (i.e. drunk, sad, weird)
+ Made in RPG Maker, even though it doesn't look like it.
Cons:

- In combat, the "hit" sound is default from RPG Maker. Could be different as the sound gets saturating after being used in so many games;
- Low resolution and some problems due to the limitations of the RPG Maker engine;
- Pain mode's too easy, and it only adds about 4 new enemies, 1 area to the game, and a different ending, unfortunately;

